  "result": "All five tests pass.\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n5 passed in 0.11s\n```\n\n**What I did:** created `kvstore/store.py` implementing the `Store` class from SPEC.md. The package `__init__.py` and the tests were left untouched. Nothing is committed since you did not ask for a commit.\n\n**Approach chosen:** Approach B, SQLite via the standard `sqlite3` module. It gives transactional, indexed key lookups that scale without loading the whole store into memory, and the default rollback-journal mode still satisfies the single-file constraint because the temporary journal is removed after each commit.\n\n**Implementation notes:**\n- One table with the key as primary key. Each set or delete commits immediately, so a reopened store sees prior writes.\n- Keys are sorted in Python so ordering follows Unicode code points rather than SQLite collation.\n- Methods raise `ValueError` if used after `close()`. The class also supports the `with` statement, closing on exit.",
